From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 14:25:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: enable downstream PPE offload from probe

Downstream (PON->LAN) hardware offload on AN7581 requires GDM2's
FWD_CFG to route PON ingress through PPE2, which airoha_dev_open()
configures. Two things break that from happening on cold boot:

1. airoha_dev_open() picks GDM2's PSE port via airoha_ppe_is_enabled(
   eth, 1), which reads the live PPE2 enable bit. Upstream commit
   cedc1bf327de ("net: airoha: Delay offloading until all net_devices
   are fully registered") defers NPU firmware load (which flips that
   bit) until userspace installs flowtable rules, so when
   airoha_dev_open() runs first it latches FWD_CFG to PPE1.

2. On OpenWrt builds, userspace only configures the logical `pon`
   netdev; eth0 (the GDM2 data-plane netdev) stays administratively
   DOWN so airoha_dev_open() never runs at all and GDM2 FWD_CFG
   retains its hardware default.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c |   18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2219,7 +2219,7 @@ static int airoha_dev_open(struct net_de
 	airoha_qdma_start(qdma);
 
 	if (!airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev) &&
-	    airoha_ppe_is_enabled(eth, 1))
+	    eth->soc->num_ppe >= 2)
 		pse_port = FE_PSE_PORT_PPE2;
 	airoha_set_gdm_port_fwd_cfg(eth, REG_GDM_FWD_CFG(port->id),
 				    pse_port);
@@ -4186,6 +4186,33 @@ static int airoha_register_gdm_devices(s
 
 	set_bit(DEV_STATE_REGISTERED, &eth->state);
 
+	/* Auto bring-up the GDM2 netdev (PON MAC, exposed as eth0). Userspace
+	 * typically configures only the logical pon interface; eth0 stays
+	 * DOWN and airoha_dev_open() never runs, leaving GDM2 FWD_CFG at its
+	 * hardware default and breaking downstream PPE offload.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(eth->ports); i++) {
+		struct airoha_gdm_port *port = eth->ports[i];
+		int j;
+
+		if (!port || port->id != AIROHA_GDM2_IDX)
+			continue;
+
+		for (j = 0; j < ARRAY_SIZE(port->devs); j++) {
+			struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev = port->devs[j];
+			struct net_device *netdev;
+
+			if (!dev)
+				continue;
+
+			netdev = netdev_from_priv(dev);
+			rtnl_lock();
+			dev_change_flags(netdev, netdev->flags | IFF_UP,
+					 NULL);
+			rtnl_unlock();
+		}
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
